<title>HONG KONG: Australia's Telstra seen issuing French franc bond.</title>
<headline>Australia's Telstra seen issuing French franc bond.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian telecommunications giant Telstra Corp has mandated Banque Nationale de Paris (BNP) and J.P. Morgan to pre-market a French franc Eurobond issue, BNP said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The issue is expected to be about 1.5 billion French francs and would likely carry a tenor of 10 years.</p>
<p>If market conditions were right, an issue would probably be launched within the next two weeks, BNP said.</p>
<p>The bond would be the first French franc issue for an Australian entity.</p>
<p>($1 = 5.1 francs)</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
